  "limits": [
    "Expansion is explicit; derived private scalars may fall outside seed bounds. Overlapping seeds retain separate observations.",
    "Current candidate-index limit is 6*N+1 <= curve order; larger seed ranges require separate jobs. No silent truncation.",
    "Default none and old configuration versions 1/2/3 retain their identities; orbit uses versions 4/5 with existing schema 7.",
    "No BSGS/minikey expansion, extra traversal mapping, throughput claim, fleet scaling, new partition certification or public deployment.",
    "All three kernels checked on native HIP/CUDA; stepped spot checks exercise each of eight visible ordinals. This is not an exhaustive kernel-by-ordinal product.",
    "Sanitizers cover five focused host/portable/storage/coordinator gates, not the complete application or device code.",
    "CUDA search and integration used separate immutable binaries and overlapped. The documented example used a separate checkout with the integration binary."
  ],
